---
description: Answering a government or housing-authority solicitation (RFP, bid, proposal, price schedule, HUD forms, Section 3, contract or insurance review)
alwaysApply: false
---

Reusable procedures for this live in `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. Open the one that matches before starting:

- `rfp-response` — extract and reconcile the solicitation, requirement register, questions to the agency, writing to the evaluation criteria, unit-price workbook, forms, assembly and the placeholder gate.
- `gov-contract-review` — clause-by-clause risk, insurance gap table, flow-down checklist, negotiation language.
- `hud-pha-procurement` — HUD and housing-authority forms and certifications; what each commits the firm to.

Non-negotiable: never invent a fact, credential, reference, insurance limit or price; unknown stays a yellow `[[FILL: ...]]` flag. Attestations (debarment, boycott, MBE/WBE/HUB/Section 3 status, no-collusion) belong to the signer. Company-specific data never goes into this public repository. See `AGENTS.md`.
